3.2 **Enforceability of Restrictive Covenants:** Section 10 (Non-Solicitation) is fully valid and enforceable as a reasonable commercial covenant under Delaware law [DOC-009#c004]. 3.3 **Liability Caps and Consequential Damages:** Section 8.1 (Consequential Damages Waiver) and Section 8.2 (12-month Fee Cap) are enforceable to the maximum extent permitted by law, with exceptions limited exclusively to actual intentional fraud pursuant to Section 8.3 [DOC-009#c004]. - **Quorum Requirements:** A minimum cluster size of 5 control nodes is required for active production regions [DOC-002#c002]. Quorum is defined as `floor(N/2) + 1`, necessitating at least 3 surviving control nodes for leader election and state commitment [DOC-002#c002]. 3.2 **Security Incident Notification to Customer:** In the event of a confirmed Personal Data Breach impacting Customer Data, Vendor shall notify Customer in writing without undue delay, and in any event within forty-eight (48) hours of becoming aware of the incident [DOC-007#c004]. 3.3 **Regulatory Reporting Timelines:** Customer acknowledges that reporting obligations to regulatory authorities (such as the EU 72-hour notice under GDPR Article 33 or relevant state attorneys general under CCPA) remain the legal responsibility of Customer as Controller, assisted by Vendor's incident report [DOC-007#c004]. Limitation of Liability and Consequential Damages
8.1 **Consequential Damages Waiver:** SUBJECT TO SECTION 8.3, NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE TO THE OTHER FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, PUNITIVE, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOSS OF PROFITS, LOSS OF REVENUE, LOSS OF GOODWILL, OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THIS AGREEMENT, REGARDLESS OF THE THEORY OF LIABILITY AND EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES [DOC-006#c009]. 8.3 **Express Carveouts from Liability Caps:** THE LIMITATIONS AND EXCLUSIONS IN SECTION 8.1 AND SECTION 8.2 SHALL NOT APPLY TO:
  (a) EITHER PARTY'S BREACH OF CONFIDENTIALITY OBLIGATIONS UNDER SECTION 5;
  (b) EITHER PARTY'S INDEMNIFICATION OBLIGATIONS UNDER SECTION 7;
  (c) EITHER PARTY'S GROSS NEGLIGENCE, WILLFUL MISCONDUCT, OR INTENTIONAL FRAUD; OR
  (d) DAMAGES THAT CANNOT BE CONTRACTUALLY LIMITED UNDER APPLICABLE MANDATORY LAW OF THE CHOSEN JURISDICTION [DOC-006#c009].
